ArgoCD Installation and Configuration Script Documentation
Overview

This script automates the installation and configuration of ArgoCD with GitLab integration. It sets up a complete CI/CD pipeline that connects your GitLab repository to Kubernetes cluster via ArgoCD.
Script Components
1. Color Coding and Utilities
bash

# Define colors for output formatting
GREEN='\033[0;32m'
BLUE='\033[0;34m'
RED='\033[0;31m'
NC='\033[0m'  # No Color

# Utility functions for formatted output
info() { echo -e "${BLUE}[INFO] $1${NC}"; }
success() { echo -e "${GREEN}[SUCCESS] $1${NC}"; }
error() { echo -e "${RED}[ERROR] $1${NC}"; }

Purpose: Provides visual distinction between different types of messages in the script output.
2. Configuration Variables

GITLAB_TOKEN="${GITLAB_TOKEN}"  # GitLab access token from environment variable

Purpose: Stores configuration parameters needed for GitLab integration.
3. Cleanup Function
bash

cleanup() {
    info "Cleaning up..."
    pkill -f "kubectl port-forward"  # Kill existing port forwards
    kubectl delete ns argocd --ignore-not-found=true  # Delete ArgoCD namespace
    sleep 5
}

Purpose:

    Ensures a clean slate before installation
    Removes existing ArgoCD installation
    Terminates any existing port-forwarding processes

4. ArgoCD Installation
bash

install_argocd() {
    # Create namespace
    kubectl create namespace argocd
    
    # Install ArgoCD
    kubectl apply -n argocd -f https://raw.githubusercontent.com/argoproj/argo-cd/stable/manifests/install.yaml
    
    # Wait for pods
    kubectl wait --for=condition=Ready pods --all -n argocd --timeout=300s
}

Purpose:

    Creates dedicated namespace for ArgoCD
    Installs ArgoCD components using official manifests
    Waits for all pods to be ready

5. ArgoCD Configuration
bash

configure_argocd() {
    # Create GitLab authentication secret
    kubectl create secret generic gitlab-auth...

    # Configure ArgoCD ConfigMap
    cat <<EOF | kubectl apply -f -
    apiVersion: v1
    kind: ConfigMap...

    # Create Application
    cat <<EOF | kubectl apply -f -
    apiVersion: argoproj.io/v1alpha1
    kind: Application...
}

Purpose:

    Sets up GitLab authentication
    Configures ArgoCD settings via ConfigMap
    Creates Application CR (Custom Resource) for GitLab repository

6. Port Forwarding Setup
bash

setup_port_forward() {
    kubectl -n argocd wait --for=condition=available --timeout=300s deployment/argocd-server
    kubectl port-forward svc/argocd-server -n argocd 8888:443 &
    sleep 5
}

Purpose:

    Makes ArgoCD UI accessible locally
    Forwards local port 8888 to ArgoCD service port 443

Workflow

    Initialization
        Script starts by cleaning up existing installations
        Ensures clean environment for new installation

    ArgoCD Installation
        Creates dedicated namespace
        Installs ArgoCD components
        Waits for all pods to be ready

    Configuration
        Sets up GitLab authentication
        Configures ArgoCD settings
        Creates Application definition

    Access Setup
        Establishes port forwarding
        Retrieves login credentials

    Completion
        Displays access information
        Shows pod status

Key Components Created

    Namespace: argocd
        Isolated environment for ArgoCD components

    Secret: gitlab-auth
        Stores GitLab credentials
        Used for repository access

    ConfigMap: argocd-cm
        ArgoCD configuration
        Repository settings

    Application: iot
        Defines GitLab repository connection
        Specifies sync policy
        Sets deployment target

Usage

    Prerequisites:
        Kubernetes cluster access
        kubectl configured
        GitLab token set in environment

    Execution:
    bash

    chmod +x script.sh
    sudo ./script.sh

    Access:
        URL: https://localhost:8888
        Username: admin
        Password: (automatically generated)

Important Settings

    GitLab Repository Path: confs
        Location of Kubernetes manifests in repo

    Sync Policy:
    YAML

    syncPolicy:
      automated:
        prune: true    # Remove resources no longer in Git
        selfHeal: true # Auto-sync when cluster state differs

    Security:
        Insecure Git access enabled
        Skip host key verification

Monitoring

    Check pod status: kubectl get pods -n argocd
    View logs: kubectl logs -n argocd deployment/argocd-server
    Application status: kubectl get application iot -n argocd
